<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Developer Knowledge Assistant · docuctl</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script src="/app.js" defer></script></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/">docuctl <span>knowledge</span></a><span class="local">Local capstone lab</span></header>
<main><p class="eyebrow">Documentation, with sources</p><h1>Find the command.<br>Check the source.</h1><p class="intro">Ask about a deployment, rollback or token rotation. Answers use the documentation version and collection you select.</p>
<div class="workspace"><section class="question-panel" aria-labelledby="question-title"><h2 id="question-title">Ask the assistant</h2><form id="ask-form"><label for="token">Lab access token</label><input id="token" type="password" autocomplete="off" value="reader-demo-token" required aria-describedby="token-help"><p class="help" id="token-help">The bundled reader token opens the handbook. Use your configured maintainer token for operations.</p><div class="select-row"><div><label for="version">docuctl version</label><select id="version"><option>3.5</option><option>3.4</option></select></div><div><label for="collection">Collection</label><select id="collection"><option value="handbook">Handbook</option><option value="operations">Operations</option></select></div></div><label for="question">Your question</label><textarea id="question" rows="4" maxlength="512" required>How do I roll back a staging deployment?</textarea><button class="primary" id="submit" type="submit">Find an answer <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></form><p class="suggestions-label">Try a question</p><div class="suggestions"><button type="button" data-question="How do I rotate an API token?">Rotate a token</button><button type="button" data-question="Where is the configuration file?">Find configuration</button><button type="button" data-question="Who won Wimbledon?">Ask outside the docs</button></div></section>
<section class="answer-panel" aria-labelledby="answer-title"><div class="answer-heading"><h2 id="answer-title">Answer &amp; evidence</h2><span id="provider" class="provider">Connecting</span></div><p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready for your question.</p><div id="error" role="alert" hidden></div><div id="result" hidden><p id="answer"></p><button type="button" id="copy-answer">Copy answer</button><h3>Sources</h3><ol id="sources"></ol><details class="request-details"><summary>Inspect this request</summary><dl id="trace"></dl></details></div><div id="empty-state"><div class="empty-icon" aria-hidden="true">?</div><p>Start with a question about docuctl.</p><p class="help">The offline baseline returns exact passages. The optional Gemini adapter adds a short explanation using the same sources.</p></div></section></div>
<p class="footer-note">These are fictional docuctl documents for the course. The assistant explains commands; it cannot execute them.</p></main></body></html>
